  "statement": "Find the angle between the planes $\\\\Pi_{1}: x+y+z=1$ and $\\\\Pi_{2}: x-y+z=0$.",
  "solution": "Normals are $\\\\mathbf{n}_{1}=(1,1,1)$ and $\\\\mathbf{n}_{2}=(1,-1,1)$. Then $\\\\cos\\\\theta=\\\\frac{\\\\mathbf{n}_{1}\\\\cdot\\\\mathbf{n}_{2}}{|\\\\mathbf{n}_{1}||\\\\mathbf{n}_{2}|}=\\\\frac{1-1+1}{\\\\sqrt{3}\\\\sqrt{3}}=\\\\frac{1}{3}$. So $\\\\theta=\\\\arccos(1/3)\\\\approx 70.53^{\\\\circ}$.",
